# Wave T46 (Inglenook kit): poffintin — a poffin tin stack: two round tins with berry-red lids and a small berry basket at their foot, seated at the Poffin House landing's east shoulder (10,13) and west of POFFIN COOK MASA's post (18,13) — the two ends of the town tale 'Auntie's Poffin Tin' (ROSA gives, MASA stages) and MASA's own words: 'Berries in, poffins out, patience throughout.' Fully opaque: the town grass is baked in (measured #248707, tg-hearthome's rendered flat, #245107 speckle). (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T46-INGLENOOK-PLAN.md §5.)
